<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vemork</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vemork is a hydroelectric power station near Rjukan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telemark">Telemark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, opened in 1911. During the German occupation its plant was the main source of heavy water for German nuclear research, and in February 1943 Norwegian commandos sabotaged it in Operation Gunnerside. The old power station now houses the Norwegian Industrial Workers Museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vemork.jpg" alt="Vemork" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MiSi at German Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VemorkHydroelectricPlant.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
